# Project 4 — Preference Elicitation

Project 4 explores different methods for collecting user preferences for movies.

The project compares two preference elicitation designs.

## Movie Representation

Movies are represented using information from the movie dataset.

The main features include:

- IMDb score
- Release year
- Genres

IMDb score and release year are scaled using MinMaxScaler.

Genres are represented using one-hot encoded features.

Movie titles are used for displaying movies to participants.

## Design 1 — Pairwise Preference

The participant is shown two movies.

For each pair, the participant selects the movie they would rather watch.

After submitting a choice, another pair of movies can be presented.

This design provides a simple preference decision with a low amount of information required from the participant at each step.

## Design 2 — Ranking

The participant is shown ten movies.

The movies can be reordered using drag-and-drop and ranked from most preferred to least preferred.

The submitted order represents the participant's preference ranking.

This design collects more preference information in a single interaction than the pairwise design.

## User Study

The proposed study compares the two designs in terms of factors such as ease of use, interaction effort and the amount of preference information collected.

The study is described in more detail in the accompanying PDF report.

